; expect 63
; Range-constrained subtypes, SATISFIED. Every conversion below holds,
; so no check fires and the answer is ordinary arithmetic.
;
; The answer is a bitmask, one bit per fact, so a compiler that gets
; one of them wrong names the fact (as `132-contract.ax` does for
; contracts):
;
;    1  `(cast Positive 5)` converts into the subtype and answers 5
;    2  a base value passed to a `(-> Positive Int)` parameter is
;       checked on entry and answers normally
;    4  a base value returned through `(-> Int Positive)` is checked
;       at the return and answers normally
;    8  widening needs no check: `(cast Int (cast Positive 6))` is 6
;   16  a lower-only range (`range 0`) checks `>=` with no upper bound
;   32  subtype operands compute as their base: adding two `Positive`
;       values answers an `Int`
;
; The violated half is `135-subtype-violated.ax`, whose whole subject
; is the status a failed check exits with (80, the contract trap:
; a range check is enforced by the same compare-branch-trap the
; `__contract` primitive lowers to, so no new runtime is added).
; No `import`: the whole file is arithmetic and comparison.
(subtype Positive is Int range 1 .. 10)

(subtype NonNeg is Int range 0)

(:: takePos (-> Positive Int))

(fn (takePos x) x)

(:: mkPos (-> Int Positive))

(fn (mkPos n) n)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (+
    (if (==
      (cast Positive 5)
      5
    )
      1
      0
    )
    (+
      (if (== (takePos 7) 7)
        2
        0
      )
      (+
        (if (== (mkPos 4) 4)
          4
          0
        )
        (+
          (if (==
            (cast Int (cast Positive 6))
            6
          )
            8
            0
          )
          (+
            (if (==
              (cast NonNeg 0)
              0
            )
              16
              0
            )
            (if (==
              (+
                (cast Positive 3)
                (cast Positive 4)
              )
              7
            )
              32
              0
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  )
)
